{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // Policy: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [
    // GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router "RSC Mode CSRF Bypass Allows Action Execution Before
    // 400 Response" (high).
    //
    // Version facts, **re-measured 2026-08-07** (the advisory's range and first-patched version
    // both moved since this entry was written — re-read them, do not trust the previous text):
    //   - vulnerable range is now `>=7.12.0 <8.3.0` — first patched moved **8.2.1 → 8.3.0**
    //   - the 7.x line still has NO fix: `react-router-dom` tops out at **7.18.2**, inside the
    //     range (this tree is on 7.18.1, likewise inside it)
    //   - the fix requires `react-router` **>= 8.3.0**, a *different package* — react-router-dom
    //     publishes no 8.x at all, so this is a package swap plus a breaking upgrade
    // Every other react-router advisory in this tree IS fixed — 7.18.1 closes the open-redirect,
    // XSS, SSR-hydration and route-matching DoS ones.
    //
    // Why it does not apply here (**re-measured 2026-08-07**, first measured 2026-07-29): the
    // suite apex shell is a **static SPA built by Vite** and copied into the Apache document root
    // by the Dockerfile's frontend stage — `node:22-slim` is a build stage only, the runtime image
    // is `php:8.4-apache`, so there is no Node server in the image at all. `src/app/router.tsx`
    // uses `createBrowserRouter` with **element-only** routes (`element` / `errorElement`), and
    // the tree has no `@react-router/dev`, no `react-router/server`, no `createStaticHandler`,
    // no RSC entry, and no `renderToString` / `hydrateRoot` call. The advisory's attack path
    // (a server executing a route action before returning 400) has no counterpart in a
    // client-only bundle.
    //
    // Re-measuring note: a bare `grep -E '^\s*(action|loader):' src` now returns 5 hits, and all
    // 5 are **false positives** — audit-event domain fields (`suite-audit-event` mapper/model,
    // the audit CSV test, and the generated OpenAPI schema), not route-config keys. Check
    // `src/app/router.tsx` itself; that is the only file that builds routes.
    //
    // Expiry: 2026-08-31. Removed by the react-router v8 migration wave (bundled with the
    // NENE2 RR8 re-evaluation). If that wave slips past the expiry, the entry must be
    // re-argued in a PR — not silently extended.
    "GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2",

    // NOTE (2026-08-04): GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (brace-expansion) was allowlisted here until today
    // with dev-only evidence, because the nested copies had no in-line fix. They do now, so the
    // entry is **removed rather than renewed** — the vulnerability is fixed, not excused.
    //
    // GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895 then landed as a bypass of that same mitigation, with a patch in
    // every affected major line (1.1.18 / 2.1.4 / 5.0.9). `overrides` in package.json now pins
    // each line to its own patch instead of hoisting one major across the tree:
    //
    //     brace-expansion@1 → ^1.1.18   (minimatch@3: eslint-plugin-import, -jsx-a11y)
    //     brace-expansion@2 → ^2.1.4    (minimatch@5: @redocly/openapi-core)
    //     brace-expansion@5 → ^5.0.9    (top level)
    //
    // Staying inside each major is what keeps the fix safe: v1/v2 export the callable itself
    // while v5 exports `{ expand }`, so a flat `^5` override makes minimatch@3/@5 throw
    // `expand is not a function` (the 2026-07-29 landmine recorded in
    // `tests/toolchain/brace-expansion-override.test.ts`, which still guards this).
  ],
}
